<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John of Montfort</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1283</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John of Montfort was lord of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyre">Tyre</a> in the crusader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-jerusalem">Kingdom of Jerusalem</a> from 1270, succeeding his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-of-montfort">Philip of Montfort</a>, who was murdered by an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/order-of-assassins">Assassin</a>. He kept the city's trade alive through truces with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> sultans. After his death his heirs held Tyre until the Mamluks took it without resistance in 1291.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-of-montfort.jpg" alt="John of Montfort" width="320" height="372" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Loyset Liédet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jan_z_Montfortu.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
